otto_table: build as a loadable module

Upstream's drivers/soc/realtek/otto_table.c is a built-in driver
(obj-$(CONFIG_REALTEK_OTTO_TABLE), builtin_platform_driver) and the rtl83xx
DSA driver now calls into it.  Out-of-tree it has to ship as a module, which
needs a real module_init and a MODULE_LICENSE: builtin_platform_driver()
expands to device_initcall(), which in a modular build becomes init_module
and collides with the DSA module's own.

--- a/otto_table.c
+++ b/otto_table.c
@@ -281,7 +281,7 @@
 		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
 	},
 };
-builtin_platform_driver(otto_table_driver);
+module_platform_driver(otto_table_driver);
 
 static int otto_table_id_to_handle(enum otto_table_id id)
 {
@@ -489,3 +489,6 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(otto_table_write_bytes);
+
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Realtek Otto switch table accessor");
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
